WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.515 --> 00:00:02.997
- [Narrator] On the
internet the other day,

00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:05.803
I found an animal that
looks like something

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:07.680
quite familiar.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.864
- They've tried to block the road,

00:00:08.864 --> 00:00:11.417
but outside of the road, one...

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:14.464
- [Narrator] Turns out, this
fluffy looking caterpillar

00:00:14.464 --> 00:00:18.631
that looks super soft is
actually super poisonous.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.443
So I called Dr. Wagner.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:24.704
He's an entomologist up at UConn.

00:00:24.704 --> 00:00:26.901
- [Doctor] My specialty is lepidoptera

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.026
which is the study of
butterflies and moths.

00:00:29.026 --> 00:00:32.055
- [Narrator] This caterpillar,
it has a few names.

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:34.487
- Well, it's megalopyge opercularis.

00:00:34.487 --> 00:00:36.866
Most people call this
animal the puss caterpillar,

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:40.258
except in the South where
many people call it the asp.

00:00:40.258 --> 00:00:41.777
- [Narrator] These
caterpillars are distinct

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:43.548
because they're covered in what looks like

00:00:43.548 --> 00:00:44.798
long soft hair.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.960
- [Doctor] Only mammals have
true hair and then what we find

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.971
on insects are really dry scales.

00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:55.950
Underneath those is where
the poison spines are,

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.627
they're maybe a little bit
like a hypodermic needle.

00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:02.015
When you pet the caterpillar
it's quite a wallup.

00:01:02.015 --> 00:01:04.842
I think of all the
caterpillars that sting,

00:01:04.842 --> 00:01:07.391
the asp may have the most painful

00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:09.013
and most toxic sting.

00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:10.762
- [Narrator] That poison
can cause headaches,

00:01:10.762 --> 00:01:15.189
swelling, nausea, blisters,
even difficulty breathing.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:16.821
And in case you were
thinking that these guys

00:01:16.821 --> 00:01:19.039
probably live deep in some jungle,

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:20.298
you would be wrong.

00:01:20.298 --> 00:01:21.802
- [Doctor] They're found mostly south

00:01:21.802 --> 00:01:24.053
of the Mason-Dixon line.

00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:25.354
- [Narrator] So here's a new adage

00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:26.943
to help you remember: 

00:01:26.943 --> 00:01:31.026
If it looks like Trump's
hair, you better beware.

